Carafe: d3d9.effectPassMerge, the switch for joining repeated passes of the game's linked effect library in Carafe's
DXVK build, is one more key the runtime copies from the program settings into dxvk.conf.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/horizon-wine/source/dxvk_options.c
+++ b/horizon-wine/source/dxvk_options.c
@@ -437,6 +437,9 @@
     OPTION( "d3d9.effectThread",
             "Carafe's DXVK build: the game's linked effect library runs on a thread of its own.",
             boolean, 30101, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, "False" ),
+    OPTION( "d3d9.effectPassMerge",
+            "Carafe's DXVK build: the effect thread keeps a pass open when the game begins the same pass again.",
+            boolean, 30101, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, "False" ),
 };
 #undef OPTION
 
